└── package.json
```

## Critical Context

- **No runtime code.** This package emits only `.d.ts`. There are no `.js`,
  `.cjs`, or `.mjs` artifacts. Consumers import types only; they bear zero
  runtime overhead.
- **Build tool**: `dts-bundle-generator` flattens the full declaration tree
  into a single `dist/index.d.ts`. Run `pnpm build` before publishing.
- **Tests are type-level.** Test files live in `tests/*.test-d.ts` and are
  run with `vitest --typecheck`. They never execute at runtime — TypeScript
  checks them statically during the test run.
- **No `dev` or `start` scripts.** There is no runtime to run. The inherited
  placeholder commands have been removed.
- **Publishing**: `private: false` in `package.json`. release-please handles
  version bumps and changelog; CI publishes to npm on merge to `main`.
- **No Azure infrastructure.** This archetype has no `infra/` directory and
  no `deploy.yml` / `infra-preview.yml` workflows.
- **Consumers must use TypeScript.** The package ships only types; it cannot
  be consumed from plain JavaScript.

